    "https://newhaven.hrmdirect.com/employment/job-opening.php?req=3824885&&#job": {
      "title": "Junior-Level Clinical Coordinator Dental Hygiene Program",
      "description": "JuniorLevel Clinical Coordinator Dental Hygiene Program - Careers at University of New Haven Career Opportunities with University of New Haven A great place to work. Careers at University of New Haven Are you ready for new challenges and new opportunities? Join our team! Current job opportunities are posted here as they become available. Back To Openings Junior-Level Clinical Coordinator Dental Hygiene Program Department: Allied Health Location: West Haven, CT Clinical Assistant Professor Junior-Level Clinical Coordinator Dental Hygiene Program Department of Allied Health Who we are: The University of New Haven, founded in 1920, is a private university whose mission is to prepare students to excel and lead purposeful and fulfilling lives in a global society. The university offers more than 150 undergraduate and graduate programs and has been recognized for academic excellence, nationally and internationally. In addition to its main campus in West Haven, the university has a campus in Tuscany, Italy. Learn more at newhaven.edu . The Dental Hygiene Program, based in the Department of Allied Health in the School of Health Sciences at the University of New Haven is seeking to hire a full-time Non-Tenure Track Faculty. This faculty member will teach in the Associate in Science and Bachelor of Science Dental Hygiene Programs and supervise junior-level clinical experiences according to the accreditation standards established by ADA CODA. The successful candidate will be committed to academic and scholarly excellence, continuous improvement through professional development, and self-assessment. This position is to begin Spring 2027. The University of New Haven’s School of Health Sciences (SHS) is one of the most progressive health sciences schools in the United States for its approach to integrating all health professionals – from technicians to physicians – in an interdisciplinary, interprofessional educational experience focused on public health, ethics, and health technology. Students develop the competencies necessary to be a successful healthcare professional in the 21st century through hands-on experiences and a curriculum focused on healthcare innovation, systems thinking, and using evidence-based approaches to solve today’s biggest challenges in healthcare. The School of Health Sciences includes the Departments of Allied Health, Population Health and Leadership, and Rehabilitation Sciences and Wellness. You will: Teach in the Associate in Science and Bachelor of Science dental hygiene programs both didactic and clinical courses Communicate with and manage outside clinical sites, maintain and update site contacts, requirements and paperwork, prepare clinic rotation schedules, address student-related or instructor-related site issues Conduct instructor calibration meetings, orientation and training. Coordinate University of New Haven Dental Hygiene Center clinic rotations, ensure local, state and federal compliance, and maintain responsive communication with students and instructors. Serve on departmental, school, and university level committees Advise and support students Maintain currency in the Dental Hygiene discipline and teaching methodologies Maintain compliance with the American Dental Association Commission on Dental Accreditation and submits reports and data as needed Other duties as directed You need: Earned Master’s degree in Dental Hygiene or an appropriate terminal degree in their discipline Minimum 3 years of clinical teaching and 1 year of didactic teaching experience in a dental hygiene program Experience with clinical coordination preferred Current Connecticut dental hygiene license, eligibility for dental hygiene licensure in Connecticut, and certification in local anesthesia Knowledge of dental hygiene accreditation, technology common in dental hygiene practice and education, and computer applications commonly used in dental hygiene Employment is contingent upon successfully passing a background investigation and proof of Connecticut Dental Hygiene Licensure. Application Instructions: All information on candidates will be kept confidential. Review of applications will start immediately and continue until the position is filled. Qualified candidates should submit: 1) a cover letter describing their academic and/or industrial experiences relevant to the position, 2) a curriculum vitae, 3) a statement of teaching philosophy, and 4) contact information for at least three professional references (reference checks will not occur without permission). What’s In It for You: Health & Welfare Programs: Employees and their eligible family members, including spouses and dependent are eligible for Medical, Dental, Vision and Life Programs. Wellness & Fitness: On-campus Recreation and Fitness Center for employees and families; Employee Assistant Program Commitment to Educational Excellence: Tuition assistance for employees and eligible dependents; Tuition exchange opportunities Employee Discounts on products, services and educational opportunities Work/Life Benefits: Generous paid time off programs; progressive paid holiday schedule (including holiday break between Christmas and New Year’s); 4 weeks of parental paid leave; flexible work schedules including summer hours where applicable Join an academic community of dedicated & supportive colleagues *The University of New Haven is not a qualifying E-Verify employer and its use of E-Verify is limited to specific government projects. For that reason, candidates with STEP OPT authorization cannot be considered for employment. Note: The budgeted salary for this position is $65,000. UNH is an Equal Opportunity Employer START YOUR APPLICATION 300 Boston Post Road West Haven, CT 06516 Visit Our Home Page © 2026 University of New Haven Applicant Tracking System Powered by"
    },
    "https://newhaven.hrmdirect.com/employment/job-opening.php?req=3805774&&#job": {
      "title": "Assistant Director Undergraduate Admissions",
      "description": "Assistant Director Undergraduate Admissions - Careers at University of New Haven Career Opportunities with University of New Haven A great place to work. Careers at University of New Haven Are you ready for new challenges and new opportunities? Join our team! Current job opportunities are posted here as they become available. Back To Openings Assistant Director Undergraduate Admissions Department: Admissions Location: West Haven, CT Assistant Director of Undergraduate Admissions - Enrollment Management Who we are: The University of New Haven, founded in 1920, is a private university whose mission is to prepare students to excel and lead purposeful and fulfilling lives in a global society. The university offers more than 150 undergraduate and graduate programs and has been recognized for academic excellence, nationally and internationally. In addition to its main campus in West Haven, the university has a campus in Tuscany, Italy. Learn more at newhaven.edu . Reporting to the Director of Recruitment, the Assistant Director of Admissions will manage a travel territory, create a travel schedule, and attend college fairs and high school visits both in person and virtually representing the university. The individual will be responsible for application review and follow up efforts. In addition, work on-campus recruitment events and daily information sessions. You are: Committed to enrolling and retaining a diverse student body An excellent communicator and connector, with the ability to interact with a diverse population of prospective students, faculty and staff Customer-oriented and able to provide the best experience to all prospective students You will: Assist in the identification, recruitment, and enrollment of prospective students from a geographic territory Conduct enthusiastic on-campus, off-campus and virtual information sessions while working special recruitment events throughout the year Represent the University of New Haven at college fairs, college nights and virtual programs throughout the year Provide admission counseling to prospective students and be responsible for day-to-day communication with students in person, via telephone, zoom, text or email Be responsible for carrying out aspects of the admission and recruitment process including, but not limited to, planning and executing fall and spring recruitment travel Coordinate time-sensitive application workflow and process applications, including the evaluation of candidates for admissions, utilizing university guidelines to determine admissibility of students and ensuring that accepted students receive appropriate communication Counsel prospective students, parents and guidance professionals throughout the college application and selection process Perform other duties as assigned and necessary in order to meet the mission of the University and the school’s enrollment goals You need: A Bachelor's degree is required; Master’s Degree preferred The ability to represent the University of New Haven in a variety of situations and be able to competently interact with a diverse population of prospective students, faculty and staff Excellent interpersonal and written communication skills Excellent organizational, planning, and project management skills A high level of technical skills and proficiency in Microsoft suite of products required The ability to travel on behalf of the University representing the school at various recruitment events A valid driver's license The ability to lift up to 50 pounds is required for the travel component of the position The ability to work evening and weekends, as needed What’s In It for You: Health & Welfare Programs: Employees and their eligible family members, including spouses and dependent are eligible for Medical, Dental, Vision and Life Programs. Wellness & Fitness: On-campus Recreation and Fitness Center for employees and families; Employee Assistant Program Commitment to Educational Excellence: Tuition assistance for employees and eligible dependents; Tuition exchange opportunities Employee Discounts on products, services and educational opportunities Work/Life Benefits: Generous paid time off programs; progressive paid holiday schedule (including holiday break between Christmas and New Year’s); 4 weeks of parental paid leave; flexible work schedules including summer hours where applicable START YOUR APPLICATION 300 Boston Post Road West Haven, CT 06516 Visit Our Home Page © 2026 University of New Haven Applicant Tracking System Powered by"
    },
    "https://newhaven.hrmdirect.com/employment/job-opening.php?req=3803156&&#job": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Practice",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Practice  Forensic Science - Careers at University of New Haven Career Opportunities with University of New Haven A great place to work. Careers at University of New Haven Are you ready for new challenges and new opportunities? Join our team! Current job opportunities are posted here as they become available. Back To Openings Assistant Professor of Practice - Forensic Science Department: Forensic Science Location: West Haven, CT Who we are: The University of New Haven, founded in 1920, is a private university whose mission is to prepare students to excel and lead purposeful and fulfilling lives in a global society. The university offers more than 150 undergraduate and graduate programs and has been recognized for academic excellence, nationally and internationally. In addition to its main campus in West Haven, the university has a campus in Tuscany, Italy. Learn more at newhaven.edu . University of New Haven is home to one of the oldest and well-respected forensic science programs in the United States. Our graduates can be located in forensic science laboratories throughout the US and abroad. We have newly renovated lab space as well as the recent addition of a high-tech Henry Lee Institute of Forensic Science facility. Modern equipment, including various DNA analysis platforms, SEM, XRD, Raman Spectroscopy, GC/MS, LEEDS comparison microscopy, etc. are available for teaching and research. The Department of Forensic Science at the University of New Haven invites applications for a Non-Tenure-Track (NTT) faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor of Practice. The successful candidate will be required to teach both undergraduate and graduate-level courses in forensic science, forensic scene investigation, and related topics. We are seeking a dedicated professional with a strong background in practical forensic scene investigation and reconstruction, active professional certifications, including IAI, POST, or other relevant certifications, and a commitment to excellence in university-level teaching and student mentorship. Special consideration will be given to candidates with proficiency in specialized documentation tools and software. You will: The successful candidate will be responsible for curriculum development and modification of existing and new core curriculum and electives, including laboratory-designated courses. The successful candidate will also be responsible for academic and career advising for undergraduate forensic science students. The successful candidate may supervise graduate/undergraduate research, Capstone, or thesis projects involving applied forensic techniques and technologies. You need: Minimum Qualifications: Education: A Master’s Degree (MS) in Forensic Science, Forensic Technology, or a closely related discipline from an accredited institution. Teaching: Demonstrated capability or background delivering lectures, instruction, or training modules in forensic science topics. Preferred Qualifications: Practical & Law Enforcement Background: Extensive hands-on experience in law enforcement, active crime scene investigation, or leadership within a state/federal forensic services unit or crime laboratory. Demonstrated expertise in forensic scene documentation, shooting reconstruction, 3D laser scanning, friction ridge examination, and evidence management. Certifications: Professional certifications through recognized bodies, such as the International Association for Identification (IAI) or vendor/technical certifications. Teaching & Instruction Experience: Prior experience as a university instructor, adjunct faculty member, guest lecturer, or academy trainer. Track record of curriculum delivery across various levels of instruction (undergraduate, graduate, professional in-service, or cooperative workshops). Specialized Knowledge: Proficiency in specialized documentation tools and software Required Application Materials: Cover Letter detailing relevant operational experience, professional certifications, and teaching background. Curriculum Vitae (CV). Statement of Teaching Philosophy. Contact Information for Three Professional References. What’s In It for You: Health & Welfare Programs: Employees and their eligible family members, including spouses and dependent are eligible for Medical, Dental, Vision and Life Programs. Wellness & Fitness: On-campus Recreation and Fitness Center for employees and families; Employee Assistant Program. Commitment to Educational Excellence: Tuition assistance for employees and eligible dependents; Tuition exchange opportunities. Employee Discounts on products, services and educational opportunities. Work/Life Benefits: Generous paid time off programs; progressive paid holiday schedule (including holiday break between Christmas and New Year’s); 4 weeks of parental paid leave; flexible work schedules including summer hours where applicable. *The University of New Haven is not a qualifying E-Verify employer and its use of E-Verify is limited to specific government projects. For that reason, candidates with STEP OPT authorization cannot be considered for employment. START YOUR APPLICATION 300 Boston Post Road West Haven, CT 06516 Visit Our Home Page © 2026 University of New Haven Applicant Tracking System Powered by"
    },
    "https://newhaven.hrmdirect.com/employment/job-opening.php?req=3803681&&#job": {
      "title": "Executive Director of Research Admininistration",
      "description": "Executive Director of Research Admininistration - Careers at University of New Haven Career Opportunities with University of New Haven A great place to work. Careers at University of New Haven Are you ready for new challenges and new opportunities? Join our team! Current job opportunities are posted here as they become available. Back To Openings Executive Director of Research Admininistration Department: Office Provost/VP Academic Affairs Location: West Haven, CT Who we are: The University of New Haven, founded in 1920, is a private university whose mission is to prepare students to excel and lead purposeful and fulfilling lives in a global society. The university offers more than 150 undergraduate and graduate programs and has been recognized for academic excellence, nationally and internationally. In addition to its main campus in West Haven, the university has a campus in Tuscany, Italy. Learn more at newhaven.edu . The University of New Haven is seeking an experienced, highly motivated, hands-on research administrator to lead the collegial and knowledgeable team in the Office of Grants and Sponsored Programs and to support the University’s continued growth in areas of research and external funding. The position is responsible for leading the Office of Grants and Sponsored Programs (OGSP), overseeing all aspects of proposal review and submission, facilitating negotiation of award terms and conditions, and identifying and resolving issues through the life-cycle of an award. The Executive Director will be responsible for responding to the needs of researchers, supporting research processes, infrastructure, and procedures, and working collaboratively with faculty, staff, and administrators to foster a positive, productive, and growing research environment. The Executive Director collaborates with the Office of the Provost, Deans, the Business Office, the Finance Director of Sponsored Programs and other leaders as well as external sponsors and agencies to ensure compliance with funder requirements and cooperation in the execution and management of sponsored programs/projects. The Executive Director will be responsible for collaborating with other research stakeholders on issues such as research agreements, fee-for-service contracts, material transfers, confidentiality/non-disclosure agreements, sub-award management, export controls, and FCOI. The position is responsible for maintaining knowledge of and responding to changes in federal government requirements, sponsor terms and conditions, and shifting levels of sponsor funding. The Executive Director will lead strategic planning and policy development for OGSP and will develop goals, objectives, and strategies and operational plans in accordance with the direction of the strategic plan. You will: Strategic Leadership & Administration Provide vision, direction, and operational management for the Office of Grants and Sponsored Programs (OGSP), including supervision and professional development of all office staff. Develop and implement policies, procedures, and systems for the administration of sponsored programs consistent with federal regulations (2 CFR 200 Uniform Guidance), sponsor requirements, and institutional priorities. Collaborate with the Provost, Deans, and academic department chairs to align sponsored programs strategy with institutional research goals and the University strategic plan. Oversee all aspects of proposal review and submission, negotiating award terms and conditions and resolving issues throughout the award life cycle. Serve as institutional liaison to federal agencies, private foundations, and corporate sponsors on matters of policy, compliance, and relationship management. Respond to researcher needs and support research processes, infrastructure, and procedures in collaboration with faculty, staff, and administrators. Oversee the OGSP operating budget, and report regularly to institutional leadership on research activity metrics. Lead the development and maintenance of the institution's F&A cost rate agreement in coordination with the cognizant federal agency and institutional finance leadership. Allocate staff workload to maximize OGSP effectiveness and ensure appropriate resource allocation. Implement Artificial Intelligence where appropriate in alignment with University initiatives. Perform other related duties as assigned. Compliance & Risk Management Serve as the institution's primary point of accountability for compliance with all federal, state, and sponsor regulations governing sponsored programs, including Uniform Guidance, agency-specific requirements, and research integrity standards. Serve as the institutional point of contact for export control policy and administration, ITAR registration, intellectual property requests, and technology transfer inquiries. Coordinate the institution's human subjects research administration in conjunction with the Chair of the IRB committee, ensuring Federalwide Assurance (FWA) compliance, protocol coordination with active awards, and appropriate training for research personnel. Manage institutional risk related to sponsored programs, including identification of compliance vulnerabilities, development of mitigation strategies, and coordination with internal audit and legal counsel as appropriate. Ensure timely and accurate institutional reporting to federal and other sponsors, including FFATA/FSRS subaward reporting, Single Audit preparation, and closeout documentation. Oversee export controls, conflict of interest disclosures, and responsible conduct of research (RCR) training in coordination with relevant institutional offices. Track, disseminate, and respond to changes in federal government requirements, sponsor terms and conditions, funding trends, and local, state, and federal regulations affecting sponsored programs administration. Faculty & Stakeholder Engagement Serve as primary advisor to principal investigators on sponsored programs matters, providing guidance on complex compliance issues, sponsor relationships, and research administration strategy. Collaborate with principal investigators on budget development and proposal submissions. Develop and deliver faculty training and outreach programs on sponsored programs policies, procedures, and funding opportunities. Partner with research stakeholders on research agreements, fee-for-service contracts, material transfer agreements, confidentiality/non-disclosure agreements, sub-award management, export controls, and financial conflict of interest (FCOI) matters. Establish and maintain clear protocols with the Office of Advancement for the handoff of private foundation awards and with the Office of Innovation for corporate awards carrying sponsored program obligations, ensuring appropriate administrative oversight. Collaborate with the Business Office and Finance Director of Sponsored Programs to ensure compliance and cooperation in the execution and management of sponsored programs. Represent the institution in professional organizations including NCURA (National Council of University Research Administrators) and relevant regional networks. Signatory Authority Serve as the institution's Authorized Organizational Representative (AOR) for all proposal submissions and award acceptances. Execute grant agreements, contracts, subaward agreements, memoranda of understanding, and other sponsored program instruments on behalf of the institution. Negotiate award terms and conditions with federal agencies, state agencies, and private sponsors to protect institutional interests while advancing the research mission. You need: Bachelor's degree required; Master's degree strongly preferred in research administration, public administration, business, or a related field. Minimum of 8 years of progressively responsible experience in sponsored programs or research administration in a higher education setting, including at least 3 years in a supervisory or leadership role. Significant experience in pre-award and non-financial post-award areas and an understanding of post-award financial management; Knowledge of compliance issues and implementation strategies; Ability to communicate effectively across a wide range of constituencies; Excellent time management skills and attention to detail The Executive Director must have a hands-on style working with faculty on budget development and proposal submissions and day-to-day tasks in this very busy five-person office. External funding support includes federal, state, other governmental agencies, foundations, non-profit community organizations, corporate contracts, and collaborative agreements with other institutions of higher education. Technical skills include Microsoft Office (Word, Excel, PowerPoint), some knowledge of Banner or equivalent system, database such as Cayuse or DataWarehouse, and experience with sponsor portals including Research.Gov and Grants.Gov. Applications will be reviewed as they are received until the position is filled. For additional information contact Dr. Ronald Harichandran, Vice Provost for Research (rharichandran@newhaven.edu). Application materials must include: a cover letter, a resume/CV, and contact information for three professional references What's in it for you: Health & Welfare Programs: Employees and their eligible family members, including spouses and dependent are eligible for Medical, Dental, Vision and Life Programs. Wellness & Fitness: On-campus Recreation and Fitness Center for employees and families; Employee Assistant Program Commitment to Educational Excellence: Tuition assistance for employees and eligible dependents; Tuition exchange opportunities Employee Discounts on products, services and educational opportunities Work/Life Benefits: Generous paid time off programs; progressive paid holiday schedule (including holiday break between Christmas and New Year’s); 4 weeks of parental paid leave; flexible work schedules including summer hours where applicable *The University of New Haven is not a qualifying E-Verify employer and its use of E-Verify is limited to specific government projects. For that reason, candidates with STEM OPT authorization cannot be considered for employment. START YOUR APPLICATION 300 Boston Post Road West Haven, CT 06516 Visit Our Home Page © 2026 University of New Haven Applicant Tracking System Powered by"
    },
    "https://newhaven.hrmdirect.com/employment/job-opening.php?req=3801787&&#job": {
      "title": "Manager Military Veterans Affairs",
      "description": "Manager Military Veterans Affairs - Careers at University of New Haven Career Opportunities with University of New Haven A great place to work. Careers at University of New Haven Are you ready for new challenges and new opportunities? Join our team! Current job opportunities are posted here as they become available. Back To Openings Manager Military Veterans Affairs Department: Office VicePresident Enrollment Mgt Location: West Haven, CT Who we are: The University of New Haven, founded in 1920, is a private university whose mission is to prepare students to excel and lead purposeful and fulfilling lives in a global society. The university offers more than 150 undergraduate and graduate programs and has been recognized for academic excellence, nationally and internationally. In addition to its main campus in West Haven, the university has a campus in Tuscany, Italy. Learn more at newhaven.edu . The Manager, Military & Veteran Affairs provides comprehensive, student-centered support for military-affiliated students, including active-duty service members, reservists, National Guard members, veterans, military and veteran dependents, and ROTC cadets. The Manager serves as the primary campus resource from inquiry through graduation for questions related to recruitment, enrollment, military and veteran educational benefits, regulatory compliance, referrals, engagement, and student success. The position leads the Office of Military & Veteran Affairs, manages the Veteran Center and VA Work Study program, and collaborates across the University to strengthen recruitment, retention, communication, compliance, and community-building initiatives. You will: Compliance, Certification and Benefits Ensure compliance with applicable U.S. Department of Veterans Affairs, Department of Defense, and state requirements, working with the State Approving Agency and Education Liaison Representative. Serve as the primary School Certifying Official and submit enrollment certifications for VA education benefits. Assist students with benefit eligibility and application processes, and maintain benefit information in applicable VA, DOD, and University systems, including the VA Enrollment Manager and related portals. Monitor legislative, regulatory, and policy changes affecting military-affiliated students and communicate pertinent updates to relevant campus partners. Serve as the primary point of contact for disbursement of the Veterans Emergency Loan Fund under Bursar supervision. Student Support and Enrollment Serve as the focal point of contact from inquiry through graduation for military-affiliated students seeking guidance on educational benefits, compliance, University resources, and campus points of contact. Serve as primary enrollment recruiter for military-affiliated students and support undergraduate and graduate recruitment efforts, recruitment events, outreach initiatives, and military- or veteran-related college fairs as needed. Partner with Student Success and Student Affairs to orient students to University life, monitor academic progress, make referrals, and share appropriate concerns through Navigate. Coordinate an outreach plan with Student Affairs and the One Stop Office to maximize communication and support for all military-affiliated students, regardless of VA educational-benefit coverage. Maintain working knowledge of Admissions, Advising, Financial Aid, Bursar, and Registrar operations and procedures to provide informed referrals and coordinated support. Office, Program and Community Leadership Manage the Office of Military & Veteran Affairs and the campus Veteran Center. Recruit, hire, supervise, schedule, and support participants in the VA Work Study program. Serve as Service to Scholar Program Director. Maintain and co-chair the Veterans Advisory Board, convene recurring meetings, and collaborate on community-building initiatives. Plan and execute the annual Salute to Service Awards Banquet celebrating student veterans and community partners. Develop and deliver University-sponsored Green Zone Training for pertinent departments and student leaders. Distribute the OMVA newsletter to military-affiliated students and, when appropriate, the larger campus community, including timely VA updates and University information. Manage military and veteran program budgets and related resources. Partnerships, Engagement and Institutional Support Serve as the University liaison for ROTC and the SALUTE Veterans National Honor Society. Advise the Charger Vets student organization and support academic, service, community-building, and recreational programs for military-affiliated students. Coordinate and lead meetings for faculty and staff involved in supporting military-affiliated students. Manage and submit surveys related to military-friendly and best-for-veterans recognition efforts in collaboration with Institutional Research. Provide staff with resources that promote excellent service and coordinated military and veteran support across campus. Support the goals and mission of Enrollment and Student Success and the University. Perform other duties and responsibilities as assigned by supervisor and Enrollment Vice President that are in accordance with the goals and mission of the University. You need: Bachelor's degree and two to four years of relevant experience. Prior service in the United States Armed Forces. Valid driver’s license and ability to travel on behalf of the University. Availability to work non-traditional hours, including occasional early mornings, evenings, and weekends. Knowledge of and demonstrated appreciation for the experiences and needs of individuals from military and veteran backgrounds. Strong interpersonal, written, and verbal communication skills, with a professional presentation and demeanor. Ability to safeguard sensitive and private information and maintain strict confidentiality. Good judgment, tact, diplomacy, discretion, reliability, flexibility, and consistent follow-through. Excellent problem-solving, organizational, and customer-service skills. Ability to work independently, collaborate effectively across departments, contribute as a team member, and meet deadlines. Proficiency with Microsoft 365 applications, including Word, Excel, Outlook, and Teams. Experience working in a higher education environment preferred. What's in it for you: Health & Welfare Programs: Employees and their eligible family members, including spouses and dependent are eligible for Medical, Dental, Vision and Life Programs. Wellness & Fitness: On-campus Recreation and Fitness Center for employees and families; Employee Assistant Program Commitment to Educational Excellence: Tuition assistance for employees and eligible dependents; Tuition exchange opportunities Employee Discounts on products, services and educational opportunities Work/Life Benefits: Generous paid time off programs; progressive paid holiday schedule (including holiday break between Christmas and New Year’s); 4 weeks of parental paid leave; flexible work schedules including summer hours where applicable *The University of New Haven is not a qualifying E-Verify employer and its use of E-Verify is limited to specific government projects. For that reason, candidates with STEM OPT authorization cannot be considered for employment. START YOUR APPLICATION 300 Boston Post Road West Haven, CT 06516 Visit Our Home Page © 2026 University of New Haven Applicant Tracking System Powered by"
